fragment_downloaded_cb({"url":"gl-egl/gstgldisplay_egl.html#gst_gl_display_egl_from_gl_display","fragment":"\n\tgst_gl_display_egl_from_gl_display\n\n\n\tGstGLEGL.GLDisplayEGL.prototype.from_gl_display\n\n\n\tGstGLEGL.GLDisplayEGL.from_gl_display\n\nCreates a EGL display connection from a native Display.\nThis function will return the same value for multiple calls with the same\ndisplay.\nThe returned GstGLDisplayEGL will *not* be marked as foreign and will free\nsome display global EGL resources on finalization. If an external API/user\nwill be also handling the lifetime of the EGLDisplay, you should mark the\nreturned GstGLDisplayEGL as foreign by calling gst_gl_display_egl_set_foreign.\nParameters:\nan existing GstGLDisplay\na new GstGLDisplayEGL\n\n\tSince\t\t\t: 1.12\n\t\t\nCreates a EGL display connection from a native Display.\nThis function will return the same value for multiple calls with the same\ndisplay.\nThe returned GstGLEGL.GLDisplayEGL will *not* be marked as foreign and will free\nsome display global EGL resources on finalization. If an external API/user\nwill be also handling the lifetime of the EGLDisplay, you should mark the\nreturned GstGLEGL.GLDisplayEGL as foreign by calling GstGLEGL.GLDisplayEGL.prototype.set_foreign.\nParameters:\nan existing GstGL.GLDisplay\na new GstGLEGL.GLDisplayEGL\n\n\tSince\t\t\t: 1.12\n\t\t\nCreates a EGL display connection from a native Display.\nThis function will return the same value for multiple calls with the same\ndisplay.\nThe returned GstGLEGL.GLDisplayEGL will *not* be marked as foreign and will free\nsome display global EGL resources on finalization. If an external API/user\nwill be also handling the lifetime of the EGLDisplay, you should mark the\nreturned GstGLEGL.GLDisplayEGL as foreign by calling GstGLEGL.GLDisplayEGL.set_foreign.\nParameters:\nan existing GstGL.GLDisplay\na new GstGLEGL.GLDisplayEGL\n\n\tSince\t\t\t: 1.12\n\t\t\n"});